    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2FTDGqZrVLEEXS9bCedsnWx)_\n\n## What\n\n- New module `sp-notes-filing` (doc: `docs/tangles/funct/sp-notes-filing.org`).\n- Pure rule `sp-notes-filing-folder`, first match wins: litnote → `litnotes/`, person → `people/`, emacs → `docs-emacs/`, docs/process/workflow/system → `docs/`, film → `objects/films/`, hardware → `objects/hardware/`, concept/zettel → `knowledge/`, anything else → `other/`.\n- `M-x sp-notes-filing-lint` (`SPC n f`) is a **dry run**; `C-c C-c` in its buffer applies after confirmation, with a backup + manifest first. `sp-notes-filing-restore` undoes a run.\n- `sp-notes-filing-mode` files a tagged note at the top of `~/notes` on save; `sp-notes-filing-run-scheduled` is usable from a timer or `emacs --batch`.\n- Denote removed: `sp-denote` module, Denote capture templates, keybindings, workbook command. Denote file names (`20240101T120000--title__tags.org`) become `20240101120000_title.org`; `#+identifier:` is dropped when the note has an `:ID:`.\n- Tags `litnote`, `film`, `hardware`, `system` added to the registry.\n\n## Not scanned\n`inbox/`, `area/`, `log/`, `workbook/`, dot folders, `inbox.org`, because other modules address them by path.\n\n## Tests\n`emacs -Q --batch -L libraries/modules/funct -l tests/sp-notes-filing-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` (8 pass). Not run against the real vault.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCLuV4PSf39usC3bgD)_",
